# Copy to .env.local and fill in from the Coveo admin console once org access is granted.
# Admin console > Organization > API Keys, and the org ID shown in the top-right org switcher.
#
# Two different kinds of values here, split by trust boundary (see
# docs/adr/0005-server-token-and-passage-routes.md):
#
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars are inlined into the client JS bundle at build time and
#   are visible to anyone who opens devtools. Only the org ID belongs here —
#   it's not a secret, it's just which org to talk to.
# - COVEO_API_KEY and COVEO_ML_API_KEY are privileged, server-only keys, read
#   only by Route Handlers under src/app/api/. Two keys, not one, because a
#   Coveo Custom API key can no longer be granted Execute queries or
#   Analytics-Push (those are now locked to predefined key purposes like
#   "Anonymous search"), while ML - Allow content preview is only grantable
#   via Custom — see src/coveo/config.ts and
#   docs/adr/0005-server-token-and-passage-routes.md. Neither may ever be
#   prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ or it would ship to the browser.
#   - COVEO_API_KEY: "Anonymous search" purpose (Execute queries,
#     Analytics-Push). Only used by /api/token in "server" auth mode (see
#     below) — not required at all in "direct" mode.
#   - COVEO_ML_API_KEY: Custom purpose, ML - Allow content preview only.
#     Used by /api/passages for Passage Retrieval, in either auth mode.

# Client-side (safe to expose in the browser bundle)
NEXT_PUBLIC_COVEO_ORGANIZATION_ID=

# Auth mode for the client search engine — see ADR-0007 and the doc comment
# on resolveCoveoConfig in src/coveo/config.ts.
# - "direct" (default if unset): the client uses NEXT_PUBLIC_COVEO_ACCESS_TOKEN
#   directly as its Search API credential — what an "Anonymous search"-purpose
#   Coveo API key is designed for (query + analytics privileges only, safe to
#   ship in client JS). Same value as COVEO_API_KEY is fine here.
# - "server": mints short-lived tokens via /api/token using COVEO_API_KEY
#   server-side (ADR-0005's original design). Requires a key with the
#   SEARCH_API/IMPERSONATE privilege — not obtainable from every org/console
#   version, verify via the privilege-introspection call in ADR-0007 first.
NEXT_PUBLIC_COVEO_AUTH_MODE=direct
NEXT_PUBLIC_COVEO_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Optional — override the search hub / pipeline names hardcoded as fallbacks
# in src/coveo/searchConfig.ts ("PokedexSearch" / "Pokedex"). Leave unset to
# use those defaults. Only useful if the admin console's pipeline ends up
# associated to a differently-named Search Hub than the code default.
NEXT_PUBLIC_COVEO_SEARCH_HUB=
NEXT_PUBLIC_COVEO_PIPELINE=

# Server-only — see the split explained above
COVEO_API_KEY=
COVEO_ML_API_KEY=
